 "format": "gai-icon/2",
 "id": "braille",
 "label": "Braille",
 "intent": "A braille display refreshes two cells of raised dots. Light: a reading wave runs left to right, column by column: each raised dot pushes up (swells) and drops back into place with a hit and a small rebound. Strong: each dot pushes up higher, drops back, then pops a second, smaller time before it settles. Every dot ends exactly where it started.",
 "//": "Two cells spelling 'on' (o = dots 1 3 5, n = dots 1 3 4 5): columns 6.5 apart in a cell, 9 between cells, rows 8 apart. Each dot is a stroked r 1.3 circle (never under half the Bold or Solid stroke, so it cannot turn inside out) over a filled r 1.4 core, so it grows with the weight (outer r 2.05 / 2.3 / 2.55, Solid 2.6) with no counter; its rig scales both, never below rest.",
